          <!-- =========================================================== Providers -->
          <section class="doc-section" id="providers">
            <h2>Providers</h2>
            <p class="lead">
              The decision protocol is provider-neutral. Pick a built-in adapter or pass
              your own; the fast pass, deliberation pass, and quality gate stay the same.
            </p>

            <div class="table-wrap">
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Provider</th>
                    <th>API</th>
                    <th>Works with</th>
                    <th>Logprobs</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>gemini</code> (default)</td>
                    <td>Google Gen AI</td>
                    <td>Gemini 2.5 Flash and compatible Gemini models</td>
                    <td>Yes</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>openai</code></td>
                    <td>Chat Completions</td>
                    <td>
                      OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, OpenRouter, Groq, Together, DeepSeek,
                      Mistral, xAI, Ollama, vLLM, LM Studio
                    </td>
                    <td>Yes*</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>anthropic</code></td>
                    <td>Messages</td>
                    <td>Claude models</td>
                    <td>Text fallback</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Custom</td>
                    <td><code>XonusProvider</code></td>
                    <td>Any model, SDK, or internal endpoint</td>
                    <td>Depends</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <p class="small muted">
              * OpenAI-compatible servers differ: some return token logprobs, some do
              not. Xonus automatically falls back to text evidence when logprobs are
              absent.
            </p>

            <h3>Gemini</h3>
            <p>
              The default provider. It uses <code>@google/genai</code> and Gemini's
              <code>responseLogprobs</code> generation option.
            </p>
            <CodeBlock code={snippets.providerGemini} lang="ts" />

            <h3>OpenAI-compatible</h3>
            <p>
              Set <code>provider: 'openai'</code> for OpenAI and any API that mirrors its
              Chat Completions shape. Set <code>baseURL</code> to the API root, including
              the version segment. This covers hosted gateways and local servers.
            </p>
            <CodeBlock code={snippets.providerOpenAI} lang="ts" />

            <h3>Local and self-hosted</h3>
            <p>
              A <code>baseURL</code> is enough for an unauthenticated local endpoint.
              Disable logprobs for text-only models; the decision still resolves, with
              zero confidence.
            </p>
            <CodeBlock code={snippets.providerLocal} lang="ts" />

            <h3>Anthropic</h3>
            <p>
              Anthropic does not expose token log probabilities. Xonus reads the final
              answer text and reports <code>confidence: 0</code>,
              <code>answerMass: 0</code>, and <code>confident: false</code>. Supported,
              but not calibrated.
            </p>
            <CodeBlock code={snippets.providerAnthropic} lang="ts" />

            <h3>Custom provider</h3>
            <p>
              Implement <code>generate()</code> for the fast pass and
              <code>stream()</code> for deliberation. A chunk is just text plus optional
              logprob steps, so wrapping a new SDK takes a few lines.
            </p>
            <CodeBlock code={snippets.providerCustom} lang="ts" />

            <h3>Environment detection</h3>
            <p>
              <code>Xonus.fromEnv()</code> reads <code>XONUS_PROVIDER</code> first, then
              falls back to <code>XONUS_API_KEY</code> and the provider-specific keys.
              <code>XONUS_MODEL</code> and <code>XONUS_BASE_URL</code> are also honored.
            </p>
            <CodeBlock code={snippets.fromEnv} lang="ts" />

            <div class="callout">
              <span class="callout-icon">i</span>
              <div>
                <p>
                  Logprobs are an optimization, not a requirement. With logprobs, Xonus
                  can measure the margin and the answer mass. Without them, it still
                  returns a decision, but sets <code>confident: false</code> and keeps
                  confidence at <code>0</code>.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- ========================================================= How it works -->
          <section class="doc-section" id="how-it-works">
            <h2>How it works</h2>
            <p class="lead">
              Xonus runs a two-pass protocol. The first pass is designed to be sufficient
              most of the time; the second exists for the cases where it is not.
            </p>

            <h3>1. Fast pass</h3>
            <p>
              Xonus maps the options to letters and asks the model for exactly one
              letter. The request uses temperature <code>0</code>, a short token budget,
              and:
            </p>

            <CodeBlock code={snippets.fastConfig} lang="ts" />

            <p>
              Every token spelling of an option letter is summed into that option's
              probability. The result is normalized over the options, while the raw mass
              is kept separately as <code>answerMass</code>.
            </p>

            <h3>2. Accept or escalate</h3>
            <p>The fast pass is accepted only when both conditions hold:</p>
            <CodeBlock code={snippets.conditions} lang="text" />
            <p>
              If both pass, Xonus returns immediately with
              <code>passes: 1</code> and <code>earlyStopped: true</code>. No reasoning
              tokens are generated.
            </p>

            <h3>3. Deliberation pass</h3>
            <p>
              Otherwise, Xonus streams a second request that asks for a short
              justification followed by an explicit marker:
            </p>
            <CodeBlock code={snippets.finalAnswer} lang="text" />
            <p>
              The stream is inspected chunk by chunk. Xonus tracks the distribution at
              every position where the generated token is an option letter, then matches
              it to the letter in the final answer marker. As soon as that margin clears
              <code>tau</code>, the underlying request is aborted. If the margin never
              clears <code>tau</code>, Xonus reads the stream to completion and returns
              the final evidence with <code>confident: false</code>.
            </p>

            <h3>4. Gate and confidence</h3>
            <p>
              At the end, two independent booleans are reported:
            </p>
            <div class="table-wrap">
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Field</th>
                    <th>Meaning</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td>decisive</td>
                    <td><code>logOdds &gt;= tau</code>. The top option is far ahead.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>gatePassed</td>
                    <td>
                      <code>answerMass &gt;= answerMassGate</code>. The model is answering
                      inside the option set.
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>confident</td>
                    <td>
                      Both of the above. This is the only field intended for automation
                      branches.
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <h3>5. Fallbacks</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>
                If the fast pass yields no usable logprobs but the text contains a
                letter, Xonus uses the text answer with <code>confidence: 0</code> and
                <code>answerMass: 0</code>.
              </li>
              <li>
                If deliberation produces no logprobs but does produce a
                <code>FINAL ANSWER</code> marker, the decision is returned with
                <code>source: "text"</code> and <code>confident: false</code>.
              </li>
              <li>
                If nothing usable is returned, Xonus throws
                <code>XonusParseError</code> instead of guessing.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <div class="callout">
              <span class="callout-icon">i</span>
              <div>
                <p>
                  <code>answerMass</code> is computed from the top
                  <code>topLogprobs</code> candidates, so it is a lower bound on the
                  model's true mass on the options. A gate of <code>0.99</code> is
                  intentionally strict; lowering it is the most common tuning step.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- ========================================================= Configuration -->
          <section class="doc-section" id="configuration">
            <h2>Configuration</h2>
            <p>
              Pass options to the <code>Xonus</code> constructor or
              <code>createXonus()</code>. Every field except <code>apiKey</code> is
              optional.
            </p>

            <div class="table-wrap">
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Option</th>
                    <th>Default</th>
                    <th>Description</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td>provider</td>
                    <td><code>'gemini'</code></td>
                    <td>
                      <code>gemini</code>, <code>openai</code> (any OpenAI-compatible
                      API), <code>anthropic</code>, or an <code>XonusProvider</code>
                      object.
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>apiKey</td>
                    <td>—</td>
                    <td>
                      Provider key. Required unless a Gemini <code>client</code>, a custom
                      provider, or a local <code>baseURL</code> is supplied.
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>baseURL</td>
                    <td>Provider default</td>
                    <td>
                      API root for OpenAI-compatible and Anthropic providers, including
                      <code>/v1</code>. Required for unauthenticated local servers.
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>headers</td>
                    <td>—</td>
                    <td>Extra HTTP headers for OpenAI-compatible and Anthropic requests.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>modelName</td>
                    <td>Provider default</td>
                    <td>
                      <code>gemini-2.5-flash</code> for Gemini,
                      <code>gpt-4o-mini</code> for OpenAI, and
                      <code>claude-3-5-haiku-latest</code> for Anthropic.
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>logprobs</td>
                    <td><code>true</code></td>
                    <td>
                      Request token logprobs when supported. Set <code>false</code> for
                      text-only models.
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>tau</td>
                    <td><code>6.0</code></td>
                    <td>
                      Log-odds margin required for early acceptance. Default is ≈403:1.
                      <code>0</code> accepts any margin.
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>answerMassGate</td>
                    <td><code>0.99</code></td>
                    <td>
                      Minimum mass on valid option tokens. Must be greater than 0 and at
                      most 1.
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>topLogprobs</td>
                    <td><code>20</code></td>
                    <td>Candidate tokens per step, 1–20.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>maxOutputTokens</td>
                    <td><code>512</code></td>
                    <td>Token budget for the deliberation pass only.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>temperature</td>
                    <td><code>0</code></td>
                    <td>
                      Deliberation sampling temperature. The fast pass is always
                      <code>0</code>.
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>escalate</td>
                    <td><code>true</code></td>
                    <td>Run a second pass when the fast pass is not accepted.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>includeRationale</td>
                    <td><code>true</code></td>
                    <td>Return the justification from a deliberation pass.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>timeoutMs</td>
                    <td><code>30000</code></td>
                    <td>Deadline for the whole decision, including both passes.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>maxRetries</td>
                    <td><code>2</code></td>
                    <td>Retries for 429, 5xx, and network failures, 0–10.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>generationConfig</td>
                    <td>—</td>
                    <td>
                      Extra Gemini generation config (Gemini only). Xonus forces
                      logprobs, temperature, and candidate count; response schemas are
                      ignored.
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>providerOptions</td>
                    <td>—</td>
                    <td>
                      Extra vendor fields merged into OpenAI-compatible or Anthropic
                      request bodies.
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>fetch</td>
                    <td>global <code>fetch</code></td>
                    <td>Custom HTTP implementation for proxies, tests, or non-standard runtimes.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>client</td>
                    <td>—</td>
                    <td>
                      A pre-built <code>GoogleGenAI</code> instance (Gemini only) for
                      custom auth, proxies, or tests.
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <h3>Advanced config</h3>
            <CodeBlock code={snippets.advancedConfig} lang="ts" />

            <div class="callout warn">
              <span class="callout-icon">!</span>
              <div>
                <p>
                  <code>responseMimeType</code>, <code>responseSchema</code>, and
                  <code>responseJsonSchema</code> are stripped from
                  <code>generationConfig</code>. Xonus needs a single letter, not a JSON
                  object.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- ============================================================= decide -->
          <section class="doc-section" id="decide">
            <h2>API · decide()</h2>
            <div class="api-sig"><span class="m">decide</span>(request: <span class="t">DecisionRequest</span>): Promise&lt;<span class="t">DecisionResponse</span>&gt;</div>

            <h3>DecisionRequest</h3>
            <div class="table-wrap">
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Field</th>
                    <th>Type</th>
                    <th>Description</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td>question</td>
                    <td><code>string</code></td>
                    <td>Required. The decision to make.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>options</td>
                    <td><code>string[]</code></td>
                    <td>
                      Required. Two to twenty-six unique, non-empty options. Order defines
