          <!-- ================================================================ FAQ -->
          <section class="doc-section" id="faq">
            <h2>FAQ</h2>

            <h3>Is Xonus an LLM?</h3>
            <p>
              No. It is a thin, typed layer over any supported chat model that turns a
              multiple-choice question into a probability-aware decision. It does not
              train or host a model.
            </p>

            <h3>Can I use it with OpenAI or Anthropic?</h3>
            <p>
              Yes. Use <code>provider: 'openai'</code> for OpenAI and any
              OpenAI-compatible API, or <code>provider: 'anthropic'</code> for Claude.
              OpenAI-compatible models that expose logprobs keep calibrated confidence.
              Anthropic returns text only today, so Xonus reports zero confidence and
              <code>confident: false</code> instead of inventing evidence.
            </p>

            <h3>Can I use a model that is not built in?</h3>
            <p>
              Yes. Pass an <code>XonusProvider</code> object with
              <code>generate()</code> and <code>stream()</code>. A provider chunk is just
              text plus optional logprob steps, so wrapping another SDK or internal
              endpoint takes a few lines.
            </p>

            <h3>Why letters instead of option text?</h3>
            <p>
              Option text spans many tokens and has inconsistent tokenization. A single
              letter gives Xonus one clean decision point whose distribution can be read
              directly.
            </p>

            <h3>What does <code>earlyStopped</code> mean?</h3>
            <p>
              It means Xonus avoided work: either the fast pass was accepted without
              deliberation, or the deliberation stream was aborted as soon as the final
              answer was decisive.
            </p>

            <h3>Why is <code>confident</code> false even though <code>logOdds</code> is high?</h3>
            <p>
              The answer-mass gate failed. The model was decisive between the top two
              options but placed too much probability outside the valid option set. Lower
              <code>answerMassGate</code>, improve the prompt/state, or review the case.
            </p>

            <h3>Does Xonus store anything?</h3>
            <p>
              No. The SDK is stateless. Requests go directly from your process to the
              selected provider using your key.
            </p>
          </section>

